sequenceDiagram
    autonumber

    participant CBDC as CBDC Core / Payment Rail
    participant TG as transaction-graph (9004)
    participant N4J as Neo4j
    participant KF as Kafka
    participant AL as alerting (9005)
    participant FD as fraud-dashboard (3000)

    participant LA as local-agent (9001)
    participant LG as local-gnn (9002)
    participant PL as privacy-layer (9003)

    participant AC as agentic-coordinator (8001)
    participant SA as secure-aggregator (8002)
    participant PM as policy-manager (8003)
    participant MR as model-registry (8004)

    rect rgb(245,245,245)
        Note over CBDC,MR: Overall Functional Flow (MVP): Data ingestion + Alerting + Federated Round Orchestration
    end

    rect rgb(232,244,255)
        Note over CBDC,AL: A) Transaction Ingestion → Graph Storage → CDC Event Stream → Alert Fanout
        CBDC->>TG: POST /transactions (transaction_id, source_account, target_account, amount, asset_type, metadata)
        TG->>N4J: MERGE(Account) + CREATE(Transaction) + relationships
        TG-->>CBDC: 200 OK (success, transaction_id)
        TG->>KF: produce transactions.events (key=transaction_id, value=tx json)

        opt Fraud Pattern Detection (Current: consumer-side)
            AL->>KF: consume fraud.alerts
            KF-->>AL: fraud alert event (alert payload)
            AL-->>AL: store recent alerts in-memory
            AL-->>FD: WS /ws/alerts (push alert payload)
        end
    end

    rect rgb(255,244,232)
        Note over FD,LA: B) Dashboard / Operator View (Polling + WebSocket)
        loop Every 5s (UI polling)
            FD->>LA: GET /agent/status
            LA-->>FD: agent status (last_round_id, last_metrics, last_update_at)
            FD->>AL: GET /alerts/recent?limit=25
            AL-->>FD: recent alerts list
        end
        opt Live alerts
            FD->>AL: WS connect /ws/alerts
            AL-->>FD: stream alert payloads
        end
    end

    rect rgb(236,255,236)
        Note over AC,MR: C) Federated Learning Round (Coordinator-driven, end-to-end)
        AC->>PM: GET /policies/global
        PM-->>AC: policy (min_agents_per_round, strategy, limits)

        AC->>MR: GET /models/latest
        alt No global model exists yet
            MR-->>AC: 404 No models found
            AC-->>AC: initialize model weights (bootstrap)
        else Global model exists
            MR-->>AC: latest model metadata (artifact_path, metrics, version_id)
            AC-->>AC: load artifact (optional in MVP)
        end

        loop Round start for each selected bank node
            AC->>LA: POST /agent/round/start?round_id=...&agent_id=...
            LA-->>AC: 200 OK (workflow accepted)
        end

        par Bank node internal pipeline (per Local Agent)
            LA->>LG: POST /train (round_id, optional global_weights, epochs)
            LG-->>LA: 200 OK (weights bytes + metrics + sample_size)
            LA->>PL: POST /privacy/apply-dp (weights bytes, noise_multiplier)
            PL-->>LA: 200 OK (dp_weights bytes)
            LA->>PL: POST /privacy/encrypt (dp_weights bytes)
            PL-->>LA: 200 OK (encrypted bytes)
            LA-->>LA: prepare update payload (weights, sample_size, metrics, timestamp)
        end

        loop Update submission (per Local Agent)
            LA->>AC: POST /updates/submit (round_id, agent_id, weights, sample_size, metrics)
            AC-->>LA: accepted=true
        end

        Note over AC,SA: Coordinator waits until expected updates received or timeout
        AC->>SA: POST /aggregate (round_id, updates[], strategy=FedAvg, noise_multiplier)
        SA-->>AC: aggregated_weights bytes + weighted global_metrics

        AC->>MR: POST /models/register (weights bytes, metrics, is_global=true)
        MR-->>AC: model version_id

        loop Budget accounting (per agent)
            AC->>PM: POST /policies/budget/update (agent_id, epsilon_spent, delta_spent)
            PM-->>AC: success + updated budget
        end
    end

    rect rgb(245,245,245)
        Note over CBDC,MR: D) Follow-up / Next Iteration (Planned Enhancements)
        Note over TG,LG: Transaction Graph can evolve to compute richer graph features (beyond basic stats) for Local GNN consumption.
        Note over SA,PL: Secure aggregation can evolve from DP-noise to MPC-style masking protocols for stronger privacy guarantees.
        Note over MR: Artifact storage can evolve from local disk to S3/MinIO + MLflow integration for lifecycle management.
    end
